Storage variable- it is a variable that is stored permanently on the blockchain.
it is persistance for transaction to transaction.
it also represent ownership.

Storage slots
 1. variable stored in contract scope allocate a storage slot.
 2. slots ade 32 bytes.
 3. solidity stores variables contiguously.
 4. reading/writing to storage is relatively super expensive to other Opcodes.
 5. variables can be packed together, automatically or manually.


 constructor function is invoked only once during the contract's deployment and never again.
 It is used fo setting up intial contract value


 there are 4 function type or visibility 
 1. private- call from within a contract.
 2. internal- call within contract + inheritance.
 3. public- call inside and outside contract.
 4. external- call from outside contract.


 
